Why this exists
---------------

Mobile application stores impose terms on the software they distribute --
limits on the number of devices and copies, restrictions to devices the user
"owns or controls", and a requirement that installed binaries be signed by the
store operator so that a user cannot install a modified build. Some of those
terms conflict with the AGPL-3.0, which forbids imposing further restrictions
(section 7) and requires that users of a User Product be able to install
modified versions (section 6). Without an explicit permission, distributing
this program through such a store would be inconsistent with its own license.

